{{- if appUsesToken .App }}
## Auth

Mode: `token`

Set the generated token before running commands that require authentication:

```bash
export OPENCLI_AUTH_TOKEN='your-token'
```

The CLI injects `Authorization: Bearer <token>` when no explicit `Authorization` header is provided.
{{- else if appUsesAKSK .App }}
## Auth

Mode: `ak_sk`

This CLI signs HTTP requests internally. Set credentials before running commands:

```bash
export OPENCLI_AK='your-access-key'
export OPENCLI_SK='your-secret-key'
```

Requests include `appKey`, `sign`, `timestamp`, and `nonce` headers. Signer profile: `{{ appSignerProfile .App }}`.

The `supplier_edi` profile uses the supplier `sha512Hex` canonical string: `method`, `/v2...` path, `appKey`, `appSecret`, `timestamp`, `nonce`, and compact `jsonBody`.
{{- else }}
## Auth

Mode: `none`

This CLI does not inject authentication headers. Use `--header` only when an endpoint needs non-auth routing or internal gateway headers.
{{- end }}

## Header Input

HTTP commands accept repeatable `--header` flags:

```bash
cargo run -- --header "ACCESS-STATUS=inner" <group> <command>
```

## Generated Skills

Each command group includes a standardized skill package under `skills/<group>/`:

```text
skills/<group>/
├── SKILL.md
├── README.md
├── assets/
│   └── demo-request.json
├── references/
│   ├── command-routing.md
│   ├── workflows.md
│   └── production-checklist.md
└── generation-report.md
```

Generated skills are API scaffolds. `assets/demo-request.json` is valid placeholder JSON and can be used immediately in documented `--file` examples; `generation-report.md` lists source documentation gaps. Before production, fill the MANUAL sections with business intent, routing rules, workflows, safety constraints, and validation evidence.
